{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Blessed be he who comes in the name of YHWH.</b> And the word ברכנוכם (we bless you) is the speech of the priests to all who come, that the blessing shall come upon them from the House of HaShem, where the Glory dwells, for you honor Him with the offerings that you bring."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 118, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:04.510413771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}